 .monthly-body{padding:20px 14px 28px}.monthly-news .augx-text{padding:20px}.monthly-news .augx-portrait img{height:220px!important}}\n\n\n.monthly-news .monthly-banner{min-height:470px;padding:44px 48px;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.65fr) minmax(250px,1fr);gap:0;background:radial-gradient(ellipse at 85% 45%,#8f603c44,transparent 52%),linear-gradient(115deg,#69182a 0%,#31171f 43%,#141315 100%)}\n.monthly-news .monthly-banner:before{inset:16px;border-color:#d8bd7555}\n.monthly-news .monthly-brand{font-size:14px;letter-spacing:.2em;margin-bottom:36px}\n.monthly-news .monthly-kicker{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.24em;color:#f0d8a8;margin-bottom:15px}\n.monthly-news .monthly-title{font-size:clamp(68px,8.3vw,112px)!important;line-height:.96!important;letter-spacing:-.045em;margin:0 0 17px!important;text-shadow:0 4px 22px #0003;position:relative;z-index:2}\n.monthly-news .monthly-title span{display:inline;color:#cda56a;font-size:.77em;letter-spacing:-.035em;margin-left:13px}\n.monthly-news .monthly-headline{font-family:Georgia,serif!important;font-size:clamp(28px,3.7vw,46px)!important;line-height:1.1!important;color:#fff1d2!important;font-weight:400!important;letter-spacing:.03em!important;margin:0 0 22px!important;padding:0!important;border:0!important;background:none!important}\n.monthly-news .monthly-summary{font-size:15px!important;max-width:470px;line-height:1.65!important;color:#d6c3b3!important}\n.monthly-news .monthly-range{display:inline-block;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.14em;margin-top:28px;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid #b8956266}\n.monthly-news .monthly-art{width:360px;max-width:100%;justify-self:end}\n.monthly-news .monthly-art:before{content:'08';position:absolute;top:-67px;right:-9px;font:italic 180px/1 Georgia,serif;color:#cfb58012;z-index:-1}\n.monthly-news .monthly-record{max-width:340px;box-shadow:0 24px 50px #000b,0 0 0 1px #d8bd7580,0 0 0 16px #d8bd7508,0 0 0 17px #d8bd7522}\n.monthly-news .monthly-label{font-size:22px;background:radial-gradient(circle,#9b3144,#62182a);border-color:#d4b475}\n.monthly-news .monthly-label small{font-size:9px}\n@media(max-width:900px){.monthly-news .monthly-banner{padding:38px 32px;min-height:410px;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.6fr) minmax(185px,1fr)}.monthly-news .monthly-title{font-size:80px!important}.monthly-news .monthly-title span{display:block;margin:10px 0 0;font-size:.66em}.monthly-news .monthly-headline{font-size:34px!important}.monthly-news .monthly-art{width:240px}.monthly-news .monthly-brand{font-size:11px}.monthly-news .monthly-label{font-size:16px}}\n@media(max-width:600px){.monthly-news .monthly-banner{display:block;min-height:440px;padding:34px 27px 30px}.monthly-news .monthly-brand{font-size:10px;margin-bottom:35px}.monthly-news .monthly-kicker{font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.18em;max-width:230px}.monthly-news .monthly-title,.monthly-news[lang=\"en\"] .monthly-title{font-size:70px!important;max-width:none;letter-spacing:-.05em}.monthly-news .monthly-title span{display:block;font-size:48px;margin:10px 0 0;letter-spacing:.04em}.monthly-news .monthly-headline{font-size:32px!important;max-width:280px;margin-bottom:18px!important}.monthly-news .monthly-summary{font-size:13px!important;max-width:260px}.monthly-news .monthly-art{position:absolute;width:200px;right:-55px;top:155px;opacity:.32;z-index:-1}.monthly-news .monthly-art:before{display:none}.monthly-news .monthly-range{font-size:9px;max-width:260px;margin-top:25px}.monthly-news[lang=\"en\"] .monthly-title{font-size:48px!important}}\n\n\n.monthly-news[lang=\"en\"] .monthly-title{font-size:clamp(48px,5.2vw,70px)!important}@media(max-width:900px){.monthly-news[lang=\"en\"] .monthly-title{font-size:56px!important}}@media(max-width:600px){.monthly-news[lang=\"en\"] .monthly-title{font-size:46px!important}}\n\n.monthly-news[data-month=\"08\"][lang=\"tr\"] .monthly-title{font-size:clamp(54px,6.3vw,86px)!important}@media(max-width:600px){.monthly-news[data-month=\"08\"][lang=\"tr\"] .monthly-title{font-size:56px!important}}\n</style>\n<div class=\"monthly-news\" lang=\"en\" data-month=\"08\" data-template=\"monthly-news-v2\"><header class=\"monthly-banner\"><div><span class=\"monthly-brand\">OLDIES RADYO · MUSIC NEWS</span><span class=\"monthly-kicker\">THE MONTH IN MUSIC</span><h1 class=\"monthly-title\">AUGUST<span>2026</span></h1><h2 class=\"monthly-headline\">Music News</h2><p class=\"monthly-summary\">Stage returns, new records and the stories that defined the month. The Oldies Radyo monthly music report.</p><span class=\"monthly-range\">1–31 August 2026 · OLDIES RADYO</span></div><div class=\"monthly-art\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><div class=\"monthly-record\"><div class=\"monthly-label\">OLDIES<br>RADYO<small>33⅓ RPM</small></div></div></div></header><div class=\"monthly-body\"><section class=\"monthly-farewell\"><h2>FAREWELLS</h2><div class=\"augx-grid\"><article class=\"augx-card\"><figure class=\"augx-portrait\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b0/Dolly_Parton_2014.jpg?utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=original&amp;utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org\" alt=\"DOLLY PARTON archive photograph\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>2014 · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dolly_Parton_2014.jpg\">Kris Harris King</a> · <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/\">CC BY-SA 3.0</a><br>Archive photo · Not taken at the August 2026 event. Displayed without cropping.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"augx-text\"><div class=\"augx-tag\">AUGUST 25 · FAREWELL</div><h3>DOLLY PARTON</h3><p>The country star died at 80. “Jolene,” “9 to 5” and “I Will Always Love You” are only part of a legacy that reached listeners across generations.</p><a class=\"augx-read\" href=\"https://oldiesradyo.com/en/2026/08/28/dolly-parton-country-music-icon-dies-at-80/\">Read in English →</a></div></article><article class=\"augx-card\"><figure class=\"augx-portrait\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a9/Frank_Beard_of_ZZ_Top_performing_in_San_Antonio%2C_Texas_2015.jpg\" alt=\"FRANK BEARD archive photograph\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>2015 · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frank_Beard_of_ZZ_Top_performing_in_San_Antonio,_Texas_2015.jpg\">Ralph Arvesen</a> · <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/\">CC BY 2.0</a><br>Archive photo · Not taken at the August 2026 event. Displayed without cropping.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"augx-text\"><div class=\"augx-tag\">AUGUST · FAREWELL</div><h3>FRANK BEARD</h3><p>ZZ Top’s drummer for more than half a century died at 77. His steady, unmistakable beat drove songs from “La Grange” to “Legs.”</p><a class=\"augx-read\" href=\"https://oldiesradyo.com/frank-beard-zz-top-hayatini-kaybetti/\">Original report (TR) →</a></div></article></div></section><div class=\"augx-grid\"><article class=\"augx-card\"><figure class=\"augx-portrait\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/90/Deep_Purple%2C_Ritchie_Blackmore_1970.jpg\" alt=\"RITCHIE BLACKMORE archive photograph\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>1970 · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Deep_Purple,_Ritchie_Blackmore_1970.jpg\">W.W.Thaler</a> · <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/\">CC BY-SA 3.0</a><br>Archive photo · Not taken at the August 2026 event. Displayed without cropping.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"augx-text\"><div class=\"augx-tag\">AUGUST 12 · LIVE</div><h3>RITCHIE BLACKMORE</h3><p>He rejoined Deep Purple onstage for “Smoke on the Water.” No permanent reunion was announced after the one-off appearance.</p><a class=\"augx-read\" href=\"https://oldiesradyo.com/ritchie-blackmore-deep-purple-33-yil-sonra/\">Original report (TR) →</a></div></article><article class=\"augx-card\"><figure class=\"augx-portrait\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/74/Sheryl_crow_%2847966331833%29.jpg\" alt=\"SHERYL CROW archive photograph\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>2019 · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sheryl_crow_(47966331833).jpg\">Zach Catanzareti</a> · <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/\">CC BY 2.0</a><br>Archive photo · Not taken at the August 2026 event. Displayed without cropping.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"augx-text\"><div class=\"augx-tag\">AUGUST · NEW ALBUM</div><h3>SHERYL CROW</h3><p>Crow announced the seven-track Pick You Up. The album was scheduled for October 9, with “Freedom Bus” among the first songs shared.</p><a class=\"augx-read\" href=\"https://oldiesradyo.com/sheryl-crow-pick-you-up-2026/\">Original report (TR) →</a></div></article><article class=\"augx-card\"><figure class=\"augx-portrait\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/27/Rod_Stewart.jpg\" alt=\"ROD STEWART archive photograph\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>archive · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rod_Stewart.jpg\">Pascal Kirchmair</a> · <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/\">CC BY-SA 3.0</a><br>Archive photo · Not taken at the August 2026 event. Displayed without cropping.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"augx-text\"><div class=\"augx-tag\">AUGUST · HEALTH</div><h3>ROD STEWART</h3><p>He postponed some concerts after a heart procedure and a period of rest recommended by doctors. Our August report records the dates as announced then.</p><a class=\"augx-read\" href=\"https://oldiesradyo.com/rod-stewart-kalp-operasyonu-2026/\">Original report (TR) →</a></div></article><article class=\"augx-card\"><figure class=\"augx-portrait\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/70/Neil_Young_Stavernfestivalen_2016_%28220929%29.jpg\" alt=\"NEIL YOUNG archive photograph\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>2016 · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Neil_Young_Stavernfestivalen_2016_(220929).jpg\">Tore Sætre</a> · <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a><br>Archive photo · Not taken at the August 2026 event. Displayed without cropping.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"augx-text\"><div class=\"augx-tag\">AUGUST · NEW MUSIC</div><h3>NEIL YOUNG</h3><p>Young announced Second Song with The Chrome Hearts. Heart and Elvis Costello also had new release news in the first part of August.</p><a class=\"augx-read\" href=\"https://oldiesradyo.com/agustos-2026-oldies-music-haberleri/\">Original report (TR) →</a></div></article><article class=\"augx-card\"><figure class=\"augx-portrait\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d6/Paul_McCartney_in_October_2018.jpg\" alt=\"PAUL McCARTNEY archive photograph\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>2018 · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paul_McCartney_in_October_2018.jpg\">Raph_PH</a> · <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/\">CC BY 2.0</a><br>Archive photo · Not taken at the August 2026 event. Displayed without cropping.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"augx-text\"><div class=\"augx-tag\">AUGUST 1 · AWARDS</div><h3>PAUL McCARTNEY</h3><p>He received his first Mercury Prize nomination, another milestone in a recording career that has continued well beyond The Beatles.</p><a class=\"augx-read\" href=\"https://oldiesradyo.com/paul-mccartney-ilk-mercury-prize-adayligi-2026/\">Original report (TR) →</a></div></article><article class=\"augx-card\"><div class=\"augx-type-tile\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"NEW RADICALS\">NEW<br>RADICALS</div><div class=\"augx-text\"><div class=\"augx-tag\">AUGUST 3 · RETURN</div><h3>NEW RADICALS</h3><p>The band remembered for “You Get What You Give” returned with a new original recording after 28 years.</p><a class=\"augx-read\" href=\"https://oldiesradyo.com/new-radicals-28-yil-sonra-yeni-sarki/\">Original report (TR) →</a></div></article></div><div class=\"monthly-notes\"><div class=\"augx-brief\"><strong>Journey</strong><p>Announced the final US leg of the Final Frontier tour.</p></div><div class=\"augx-brief\"><strong>Jethro Tull</strong><p>Announced a November 14 concert in Istanbul.</p></div><div class=\"augx-brief\"><strong>Madonna &amp; Kylie Minogue</strong><p>Their “Love Sensation” attracted attention on the UK chart.</p></div><div class=\"augx-brief\"><strong>Elvis Presley</strong><p>Elvis Week ended with the traditional Graceland vigil.</p></div><div class=\"augx-brief\"><strong>Whitney Houston</strong><p>A catalogue release and Barbie project celebrated her legacy.</p></div><div class=\"augx-brief\"><strong>Glenn Hughes</strong><p>Said he would stop live performance after medical advice.</p></div></div><div class=\"augx-strip\">From Oldies Radyo: August was more than a glance backwards. These songs live on in new collaborations, new recordings and concert halls still filled by their listeners.</div><div class=\"augx-foot\"><h2>Sources and photo credits</h2><p>These are summaries of announcements made in August 2026. Health and touring plans may have changed since. See the full News archive for updates. <a href=\"https://oldiesradyo.com/muzik-haberleri/\">News archive</a>.</p><p><a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/87156f3e6a1547b88bf414529b644ad3\">Associated Press: Dolly Parton</a> · <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/72139238d1dbf3d277bdb3b8584eecc9\">Associated Press: Frank Beard</a> · <a href=\"https://oldiesradyo.com/agustos-2026-oldies-music-haberleri/\">Oldies Radyo: August 1–10</a>.</p><p class=\"augx-credit\">Every photograph is credited and linked to its license. These are archive photographs and do not depict the August 2026 events.</p></div></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->"
